# Credential Inventory

This file records safe credential routing metadata only. It must never include passwords, API keys, bearer tokens, cookies, one-time secrets, private keys, or copied secret values.

## NuGet Publishing

- credential_id: nuget-api-key-local-file
- purpose: authenticated NuGet package push for TinyRustLM and UAIX Browser package publication
- local_secret_file: `C:\Users\AI\.codex\nuget-api-key.txt`
- expected_environment_variable: `NUGET_API_KEY`
- source_scope: NuGet package publishing
- allowed_use: read the local file only when the user explicitly requests a real authenticated NuGet push
- forbidden_use: do not print, log, copy into reports, store in package artifacts, commit, or include the secret value in `.uai` memory
- verification_rule: before publishing, verify package freshness, feed audit, SHA256SUMS binding, symbol package presence, and NuGet target source
- publish_boundary: dry runs do not need the secret; real pushes require explicit publish intent and must redact the API key from command output and reports
